{"what":"Tesla, Inc. (TSLA). This chart runs from Mar 24, 2014 to Jul 30, 2014.","setup":"The stock rose about 72% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 11 weeks, peaking at $235.73 and pulling back 25% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jun 23, 2014 it closed at $237.22, its first close above the base high of $235.80. Volume that day was 7.8M shares, 1.16x the prior 10-day average of 6.7M. It didn't hold. By Jul 7, 2014 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $228.92.","lesson":"This is an example of a false breakout. Volume on the breakout day was light, and that tell was visible before the move fell apart. Cutting it early was a good read."}}